Added `__traits(vtblSymbol)` and `__traits(interfaceSymbol)`, and `__traits(initSymbol)` now yields `SymbolSlice`

`__traits(vtblSymbol, C)` is the vtable of class `C`.

`__traits(interfaceSymbol, C)` is the `Interface[]` array of class or interface
`C`, the one `TypeInfo_Class.interfaces` refers to.

Like `__traits(initSymbol)`, they refer to symbols whose address is only known at
link time. All three now yield a `SymbolSlice!T`, which holds the length and the
address of the symbol. During CTFE its `length` and `ptr` can be used and it can
be stored, for example in static data built at compile time; only the contents
cannot be read:

---
struct S { int a = 1; long b = 2; }
class C { void f() {} }

struct Info
{
    SymbolSlice!(const void) init;
    SymbolSlice!(const(void*)) vtbl;
}

const Info info = Info(__traits(initSymbol, S), __traits(vtblSymbol, C));
static assert(info.init.length == S.sizeof);
---

Previously `__traits(initSymbol)` returned a `const(void)[]` and could not be used
during CTFE at all. Code that checks its type with
`is(typeof(...) == const(void)[])` needs updating.
